{
  "manufacturer": "Yaskawa",
  "manufacturer_slug": "yaskawa",
  "model": "GA500 AC drive (MEMOBUS/Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "ga500",
  "short_model": "GA500",
  "aliases": [
    "CIPR-GA50U",
    "GA500 Versatile Compact"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
  "applies_to": "Yaskawa GA500 drives using the built-in RS-485 MEMOBUS/Modbus port (terminal TB4), per technical reference SIEPC71061752 revision C.",
  "summary": "Yaskawa's compact general-purpose variable frequency drive with a built-in RS-485 MEMOBUS/Modbus RTU port. Run/stop, frequency reference and other commands are written to hex registers 0001H-000FH, drive status, faults and key monitors are read from 0020H onwards, and every parameter has its own hex register shown in the parameter list. This map covers the command block, status/fault words, the main monitors with fixed units, and the b1/H5 communication parameters.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 31,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "hex 0-based",
    "note": "Register numbers are printed in hex and go into the request unchanged: the manual's read example asks for starting register 0020H by sending 00 20, and its write example writes 0001H/0002H directly. Parameters use the hex number printed under each parameter in the parameter list (e.g. H5-04 = 0428H)."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": "Drive software PRG 01013, 01014 and 01015 (per the manual's revision history)",
  "source": {
    "title": "GA500 Drive Technical Reference (Versatile Compact Type)",
    "doc_number": "SIEPC71061752C",
    "revision_date": "2023-06",
    "url": "https://www.yaskawa.com/delegate/getAttachment?documentId=SIEPC71061752&cmd=documents&documentName=SIEPC71061752.pdf",
    "pages": "Section 6.3 MEMOBUS/Modbus: setup pp. 224-226, function codes and message examples pp. 228-235, Enter command p. 234, command data Table 6.15 pp. 236-237, monitor data Table 6.16 pp. 238-244; parameter list b1 p. 376 (b1-01/b1-02 = 0180H/0181H), H5 pp. 432-433, U monitors pp. 464-471"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Frequency registers (0002H reference, 0023H U1-01, 0024H U1-02) use the units chosen in o1-03 (0 = 0.01 Hz, 1 = 0.01% of E1-04, 2 = RPM, 3 = user units); o1-03's default depends on A1-02, so they are left unscaled here.",
    "Left out: 0025H U1-06 output voltage (unit switched by H5-10), 0026H U1-03 output current (Table 6.16 prints 0.1 A, but the U1-03 monitor list says its units change with drive model - 0.01 A for B001-B018, 2001-2042, 4001-4023 and 0.1 A for 2056-2082, 4031-4060 - and does not say whether 0026H follows that rule, so no single scale is safe), 0027H U1-08 output power (units differ by drive model), 0028H/0032H torque reference (sign not stated), 002FH frequency reference bias and 0068H U4-08 heatsink temperature (sign not stated; both may go negative), 003EH/003FH output frequency in r/min and % (sign not stated), 00ABH rated current and 0042H U1-03 (8192 = rated current, model-dependent units), U4-10/U4-11 kWh (resolution of the lower-digit register is unclear), 0080H-0097H fault trace/history.",
    "U4-01 cumulative operation time is available as 004CH (10 h units) or split over 0098H (value / 10) and 0099H (last digit).",
    "0040H-004AH, 004CH-007EH and 0080H-0097H carry the U1/U4/U2/U3 monitors at the hex numbers in the U-monitor list.",
    "The table example in the manual for function 67H labels 0024H as U1-01; Table 6.16 assigns U1-01 to 0023H and U1-02 to 0024H, which this map follows."
  ],
